["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG711b03ddf8d71e78926467df1c1b088027dd871978f5bfaaecdd0b6bdd5673cb","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/waves-derived-from-scope","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: Waves are derived from scope, not paired by hand\n\n## Outcome\n\n`aep artifact waves` reads `depends_on` edges and each story's machine-readable scope and prints\nthe waves that can run in parallel, exiting non-zero on a dependency cycle or two stories on one\nsurface.\n\n## Context\n\nFiled from the 2026-09-02 review of a third-party plugin, which does this in a script from a plan's\nscope lines. Here it belongs in Rust. Not scheduled; recorded so the idea has a place. Depends on\n`## Scope` becoming a frontmatter field or a fenced list the CLI can parse.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The verb exists, is deterministic, and the wave skill in the agent-plugins repository stops\n  describing pairwise overlap in prose.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nRunning the waves.\n\n## Open Questions\n\nWhere scope lives on the artifact — operator decides.\n","relations":[{"decomposes":"epic:adopter-feedback-round-2"}],"scope":[{"confidence":"inferred","path":"crates/aep-backend-markdown"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/aep-domain"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/protocol-cli"}],"status":"archived","title":"Waves are derived from scope, not paired by hand"},"lifecycle_state":"archived"}},"id":"MIG711b03ddf8d71e78926467df1c1b088027dd871978f5bfaaecdd0b6bdd5673cb","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG711b03ddf8d71e78926467df1c1b088027